// ── Rota notices: a free, instant "your shift changed" on the person's phone (Web Push, B5, John 2026-11-10) ─────
// The calendar link refreshes only every 8–24 h (Google), so a changed shift also reaches the person's own devices at
// once through the browsers' free push services (Web Push with VAPID; no paid service, no payload, no encryption):
//   - /sw.js (public): a minimal service worker with ONLY a push and a notificationclick handler. No fetch handler and
//     no caching, so registering it never changes how the app loads (every page and file still comes from the network).
//   - POST /rota/push/subscribe {staff_id, subscription:{endpoint, keys:{p256dh, auth}}} (signed in, own pharmacy;
//     the person is the one chosen on that device, E.rotaMe) → {ok, id, k}: one row per device (endpoint), a random
//     secret k kept only on the device (its SHA-256 here). POST /rota/push/unsubscribe {endpoint}. GET /rota/push/key.
//   - When a person's shifts or leave change (POST/PUT/DELETE /shifts/assignments, /shifts/apply-pattern,
