// ID card change for one person, on their details and on every one of their records
// (POST /people/:id/change-id-card, POST /people/id-card-changes/:change/undo,
//  GET /people/:id/id-card-changes). Separate block: nothing above calls into it.
//
// Safety, in the order the code applies it:
//   - Who: PEOPLE_ID_CARD_CHANGE_ROLES may apply a change; admin and staff may only preview it.
//   - Where: every read and write is `org_id = ? AND location_id = ?` of the caller. Other
//     pharmacies of the same group (same org, other location) and other orgs are never read
//     or written. Every table below has its own location_id (contacts_clients is the one
//     contacts table that does; the group-wide contacts tables hold no ID card).
//   - Which rows: a row is the person's only when its card is one of the old card's spellings
//     (mtIdCardLookupKeys) AND its name is the person's (personNamesCompatible) or blank. A row
//     with the old card under someone else's name is left alone and listed. A row with only a
//     name is never changed; "stamp" (from = "") adds the card only to rows the user ticked,
//     whose card is blank and whose name is exactly the person's.
//   - Refused: the new card already on another person (people), or on any record under a
//     different name (case B: the caller must sort out who it is first).
//   - What: only the card column (and, in JSON registers, only the card key). Never DELETE.
//   - Confirmed: the preview returns a plan fingerprint; applying with a different one (rows
//     changed in between) is refused with the new preview, so what was confirmed is what runs.
//   - One transaction (D1 batch): header, every row's old/new value (insert-only log), the
//     updates; then one audit_log entry (auditWith before/after). Undo is another insert-only change that puts back
//     only values still as this change left them.
