// The memo above lasts one isolate, and Cloudflare starts isolates often: a cold /today ran ~100 schema statements
// (2–3 s on D1, once 12 s). So each schema step also leaves a mark in the database (eikon_schema: name -> fingerprint
// of its own code). A new isolate reads all marks in one query and skips every step whose code has not changed;
// a changed step (new column, new index) runs once more. Anything odd (no table, a failed read) runs the step as before.
const __schemaMarks = new WeakMap();
function schemaFingerprint(name, impl) {
