/* ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   PRIVACY — everything we hold on one person (export), erase one person (anonymise in place, undo for 24 hours),
   and Settings › Download our records for customers, bookings, messages, money and team (gdpr block).
   Additive only: two new tables (gdpr_erasures, gdpr_erasure_rows), new routes; the router has one line per route
   next to the /people routes, and scheduled() one guarded line that wipes the undo copies once their 24 hours are up.
     POST /people/:id/privacy            what we hold, table by table: rows that are surely theirs, rows with the same
                                         name only (to be ticked), what an erase would change and what it keeps (and why).
     POST /people/:id/export { rows }    the person's rows from every table, own pharmacy only. Audited (PERSON_EXPORT).
     POST /people/:id/erase  { rows, confirm, plan, reason }
                                         no confirm: the exact plan (table, row, column) and its fingerprint. confirm +
                                         the same fingerprint: one D1 batch writes the header, the old value of every
                                         column it changes (insert-only), and the updates; then one audit row
                                         (PERSON_ERASE, counts only: never the values). Never DELETE: rows other records
                                         point at stay, with "Erased person #<id>" for the name and blanks for contacts.
     POST /people/erasures/:id/undo      within GDPR_UNDO_HOURS: puts back the values where the row is still as the
                                         erase left it, then deletes the copies. Audited (PERSON_ERASE_UNDO).
     GET  /people/:id/erasures           the person's erasures, newest first.
     GET  /export/records?part=&from=&to=&after=   Settings › Download our records (read only, paged by id).
   Who: admin of this pharmacy (GDPR_ROLES). Staff get 403, also for the preview. Where: every read and write is
   org_id = ? AND location_id = ? of the caller; table and column names come from GDPR_TABLES, never from a request.
   What stays: GDPR_POLICY, as John decided on 2026-11-11 (legal records keep the name; bookings, loyalty and messages
   are anonymised; do-not-email lists, credit notes and till receipts are kept; undo 24 hours).
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
